IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `caa-types`
IMPORT `caa-s55`

-- Civil Aviation Act 2023 — GOALS 1-3: DOMESTIC CARRIAGE AND DELAY.
--
--   "Does the domestic subpart apply; which carrier is liable; is it liable
--    for the delay; what is the most it must pay; and by when must the
--    action be brought?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2023_10.txt — ss 270-283.

§ `Goal 1 — application and carriers`

-- s 270 "(1) This subpart applies to any carriage by air ... in which,
-- according to the contract between the parties,— (a) the place of departure
-- and the place of destination are both in New Zealand; and (b) there is no
-- agreed stopping place outside New Zealand." s 271: for combined carriage
-- "this subpart applies only to the carriage by air". s 272 "This subpart
-- does not apply to— (a) any carriage by air on a single flight in respect of
-- which ... the place of departure and the intended place of destination are
-- the same; or (b) any other types of flights that are excluded ... by the
-- regulations."
@ref ss 270-272
@export Whether the domestic carriage subpart of the Civil Aviation Act 2023 (NZ) governs a passenger's delay: departure and destination both in New Zealand with no agreed stopping place outside it (s 270), the delay in the part carried by air (s 271), and not a single flight returning to its starting point or a flight excluded by regulations (s 272). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A Carriage  @desc The places of departure and destination, any stopping place abroad, the exclusions, and whether the delay was in the air part
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the domestic carriage subpart applies to` c IF
        c's `departure in New Zealand`
    AND c's `destination in New Zealand`
    AND NOT c's `an agreed stopping place outside New Zealand`
    AND NOT c's `a single flight returning to its departure point`
    AND NOT c's `excluded by regulations`
    AND c's `the delay was in the carriage by air`

-- s 273 "(a) ... (i) the contracting carrier is liable in respect of the
-- whole of the carriage contemplated in the contract ...; and (ii) the actual
-- carrier is liable solely in respect of the carriage that the actual carrier
-- performs". s 275 "If carriage is performed ... by successive carriers, the
-- contracting carrier who is liable is the successive carrier who performed
-- or was to perform the carriage where the delay occurred." So in successive
-- carriage a contracting carrier answers only for the delayed stage (added
-- after the independent pass).
@ref ss 273, 275
GIVEN f IS A `Carrier facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier is answerable for the delay` f IF
    CONSIDER f's `carrier`
    WHEN `the contracting carrier` THEN (NOT f's `carriage by successive carriers`) OR f's `performed the carriage where the delay occurred`
    WHEN `the actual carrier` THEN f's `performed the carriage where the delay occurred`
    WHEN `a successive carrier` THEN f's `performed the carriage where the delay occurred`

§ `Goal 2 — liability and its limit`

-- s 274 "(1) A carrier is liable under this section for damage caused by
-- delay in the carriage of passengers. (2) Despite subsection (1), a carrier
-- is not liable ... if the carrier proves that the delay— (a) arose by reason
-- of— (i) meteorological conditions; or (ii) compliance with instructions,
-- advice, or information given by an air traffic control service; or (iii)
-- obedience to orders or directions given by a lawful authority; or (b) was
-- made necessary by force majeure; or (c) was necessary for the purpose of
-- saving or attempting to save life." s 276 "The carrier is not liable ...
-- if the carrier proves that— (a) the carrier ... took all necessary measures
-- to avoid the damage; or (b) it was not possible ... to take those
-- measures."
@ref ss 274, 276
GIVEN d IS A `Delay claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier is liable for the delay` d IF
        d's `cause of delay` EQUALS `another cause`
    AND NOT d's `all necessary measures taken or impossible`

-- s 277 "(1) The liability of the carrier in respect of damage caused by
-- delay is limited to the lesser of— (a) the amount of damage proved ...; and
-- (b) an amount representing 10 times the sum paid for the carriage. (2) ...
-- the carrier may, by special contract, increase the amount". s 278 "(2) A
-- provision of a contract of carriage ... that has the effect of overriding or
-- limiting a carrier's liability under this subpart ... is unenforceable." s
-- 279 "The limits of liability referred to in section 277 do not apply if it
-- is proved that the damage resulted from an act or omission of the carrier
-- done— (a) with intent to cause damage; or (b) recklessly as to whether
-- damage would result." A raised limit is read as replacing 10 times the fare
-- where it is higher (fork F1).
@ref ss 274, 276-279
@export The most a carrier must pay a passenger for delay in domestic carriage under ss 274-279 of the Civil Aviation Act 2023 (NZ): nothing if the delay arose from weather, air traffic control, lawful orders, force majeure or saving life, or if all necessary measures were taken or impossible; otherwise the damage proved, up to 10 times the fare (or a higher limit agreed by special contract), with no limit for intentional or reckless damage, and no effect for contract terms that limit liability further. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN d IS A `Delay claim`  @desc The cause of delay, the measures taken, the damage proved, the fare, any special contract, intent or recklessness, and any limiting term
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the carrier must pay for the delay` d MEANS
    IF   NOT `the carrier is liable for the delay` d
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF   d's `damage intended or caused recklessly`
         THEN d's `damage proved`
         ELSE min (d's `damage proved`) limit
    WHERE
        tenTimes MEANS 10 TIMES d's `sum paid for the carriage`
        limit MEANS
            CONSIDER d's `limit raised by special contract to`
            WHEN JUST raised THEN max raised tenTimes
            WHEN NOTHING THEN tenTimes

§ `Goal 3 — time limits`

-- s 283 "An action must not be brought under this subpart against a carrier
-- later than 2 years after the later of the following dates: (a) the date on
-- which the aircraft arrived at the destination: (b) if the aircraft did not
-- arrive at the destination,— (i) the date on which the aircraft ought to
-- have arrived at the destination; or (ii) the date on which the carriage
-- stopped." Without arrival, the later of (b)(i) and (b)(ii) (fork F2).
@ref s 283
@export The last day to bring an action against a carrier for delay in domestic carriage under s 283 of the Civil Aviation Act 2023 (NZ): 2 years after the aircraft arrived at its destination, or, if it did not, 2 years after the later of the day it ought to have arrived and the day the carriage stopped. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Claim dates`  @desc Arrival, the day it ought to have arrived, any day the carriage stopped, and the day the action is brought
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to bring an action, dates` t MEANS
    `the last day under s 55 for a deadline of` (`add years` start 2)
    WHERE
        start MEANS
            CONSIDER t's `arrived at the destination on`
            WHEN JUST arrived THEN arrived
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                CONSIDER t's `carriage stopped on`
                WHEN JUST stopped THEN IF stopped GREATER THAN t's `ought to have arrived on` THEN stopped ELSE t's `ought to have arrived on`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN t's `ought to have arrived on`

@ref s 283
GIVEN t IS A `Claim dates`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is in time` t IF
    t's `action brought on` AT MOST `the last day to bring an action, dates` t

-- s 281 "(2) Person A must not bring proceedings ... to obtain a contribution
-- from person B later than 2 years after the time when judgment is obtained
-- against person A."
@ref s 281(2)
GIVEN judgment IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for contribution proceedings after judgment on` judgment MEANS
    `the last day under s 55 for a deadline of` (`add years` judgment 2)
